 "_": "Physical-material records (2.7a2, module 75 §54-55): one record per required collider material, each with the arrow response by which the world hit resolves. The four outcome probabilities sum to 1 (stick takes the remainder). `minImpactSpeedMps`: slower than this the arrow only rests (no penetration). `ricochetRetention` and `passThroughRetention`: the share of speed kept after a glance or a pass. Footstep, impact and the other responses join these records as their systems land. `climb` (2.12, botw-climbing-system.md §11a.5): `grip` dry and `wetGripMultiplier` (effective grip = grip x wetGripMultiplier^wetness x (1 + gripBonus)); `fallbackCategories`: the kit categories whose colliders with no tag and no Havok material count as this material (the survey's materialFromCategory); `variants`: the surface classes the material alone cannot tell (stoneDressed by planarity, thatch by an alpha-masked render material). `ground` (2.9c f, 0157 ruling 11): terrain-only rows that the feet read, not collider tags: the land cover names (`landCover`, the `GROUND_MATERIAL_SURFACE` names), `speedMultiplier` on every ground speed and `sprintAllowed`.",
